ent elision or fusion of vowels contracting into one sound (crasis). In preconsonantal coda position, ⟨ν⟩ may be added to create a long syllable in poetic meter. Nu is also usually written before a pause at the end of a clause in prose or the end of a verse in poetry.","dna16":"8800499140000125","ex":[],"id":"wikt:ephelcystic nu:noun:1","pos":"noun","src":"wikt","sym":"3:1,5:1,18:1,25:1,48:1,74:1,85:1,111:1","syn":[]},{"def":"Paragogic nu ⟨ν⟩ (n), understood as an allomorph of certain Greek morphemic forms otherwise terminating in vowels ⟨ε⟩ (e) or ⟨ι⟩ (i), viz. third person verb and third declension dative plural noun forms, phonemically represented as -ε(ν) (-e(n)) and -ῐ(ν) (-ĭ(n)). An early Attic–Ionic innovation, nu paragoge spread through the Hellenic world; inclusion or omission of ⟨ν⟩ in ancient inscriptions is so variable and unpredictable as to suggest morphemes with and without ⟨ν⟩ occurred in free variation, not bound to the prescriptive rules of phonetic harmony codified by later Byzantine grammarians.","dna16":"8800499140000224","ex":[],"id":"wikt:ephelcystic nu:noun:2","pos":"noun","src":"wikt","sym":"3:1,5:1,9:1,52:1,56:2,104:1","syn":[]}]},"ephelcystic nus":{"dna16":"8800499141000017","forms_of":["ephelcystic nu"],"senses":[]},"ephelides":{"dna16":"8800499142000016","forms_of":["ephelis"],"senses":[]},"ephelis":{"dna16":"8800499143000015","senses":[{"def":"Synonym of freckle.","dna16":"8800499143000122","ex":[],"id":"wikt:ephelis:noun:1","pos":"noun","src":"wikt","sym":"","syn":[]}]},"ephemera":{"dna16":"8800044791000014","forms_of":["ephemeron"],"senses":[{"def":"something transitory; lasting a day","dna16":"8800044791000121","ex":[],"id":"oewn-ephemera__1.28.00..","pos":"noun","src":"wn","sym":"48:1","syn":[]},{"def":"Especially, such objects that are collectibles, such as (originally) cheap publications (e.g., pamphlets, brochures), single-use packaging from packaged goods, and giveaway or throwaway trinkets.","dna16":"8800044791000220","ex":["vintage ephemera"],"id":"wikt:ephemera:noun:2","pos":"noun","src":"wikt","sym":"2:1","syn":[]},{"def":"Published single-sheet or single-page documents which are meant to be thrown away after one use.","dna16":"8800044791000329","ex":[],"id":"wikt:ephemera:noun:3","pos":"noun","src":"wikt","sym":"2:1,4:1,12:1","syn":[]},{"def":"Transitory audiovisual matter not intended to be retained or preserved.","dna16":"8800044791000428","ex":["video ephemera","audio ephemera"],"id":"wikt:ephemera:noun:4","pos":"noun","src":"wikt","sym":"","syn":[],"tags":["broadly"]},{"def":"A mayfly (genus Ephemera).","dna16":"8800044791000527","ex":["These names, and many more, are, in various parts of the country, applied to an ephemera, which appears in most, if not all of the Trout waters of these kingdoms, throughout the whole season, although in greater numbers "],"id":"wikt:ephemera:noun:5","pos":"noun","src":"wikt","sym":"","syn":[]}]},"ephemerae":{"dna16":"8800499144000014","forms_of":["ephemera"],"senses":[]},"ephemeral":{"dna16":"8800044792000013","senses":[{"def":"lasting a very short time","dna16":"8800044792000120","ex":["the ephemeral joys of childhood","a passing fancy"],"id":"oewn-ephemeral__5.00.00.impermanent.00","pos":"adjective","src":"wn","sym":"48:1,49:1","syn":["fugacious","passing","short-lived","transient","transitory"]},{"def":"anything short-lived, as an insect that lives only for a day in its winged form","dna16":"8800044792000229","ex":[],"id":"oewn-ephemeral__1.05.00..","pos":"noun","src":"wn","sym":"49:1","syn":["ephemeron"]},{"def":"Existing for only one day, as with some flowers, insects, and diseases.","dna16":"8800044792000328","ex":[],"id":"wikt:ephemeral:adjective:3","pos":"adjective","src":"wikt","sym":"85:1","syn":["earthly","ephemeral","brief","deciduous","evanescent","fleeting"]},{"def":"Usually dry, but filling with water for brief periods during and after precipitation.","dna16":"8800044792000427","ex":["The graben constitutes a depositional basin and 